Straight.\n\nPure Straight requires three chows and a pair \u2014 no pungs.\n\nBut I have a pung \u2014 so invalid.\n\nSimilarly, most chow-based patterns require no pungs.\n\nSo my [W5,W5,W5] pung is blocking many patterns.\n\nBut it gives me:\n- Dragon Pung? No, W5 is not dragon.\n- Pung of Terminals or Honors? W5 is simple \u2014 no.\n- So this pung scores nothing by itself.\n\nIn fact, it might be dead weight.\n\nBut I can't remove it.\n\nSo my hand is stuck with a non-scoring pung.\n\nOther patterns:\n\n- One Voided Suit: I have W (characters) and T (bamboos) \u2014 missing B (dots)? I have no dot melds, but do I have dot tiles?\n\nMy hand: W7,W8,T1,T7,T9 \u2014 no dots.\n\nMelds: all W \u2014 no dots.\n\nSo only two suits: characters and bamboos \u2014 missing dots.\n\nSo if I win, I will have One Voided Suit (1 point).\n\n- No Honors: I have no honor tiles in hand or melds \u2014 so if I win without honors, I get No Honors (1 point).\n\n- All Simples: only numbers 2-8, no 1,9 or honors.\n\nBut I have T1 and T9 \u2014 terminals \u2014 so not all simples.\n\nT1 and T9 are terminals.\n\nSo not all simples.\n\n- Pung of Terminals or Honors: I have no such pung.\n\nMy only pung is W5 \u2014 simple.\n\nSo minimal base score.\n\nI need to find a way to reach 8 points.\n\nOther options:\n\n- Chicken Hand: if I win with no other fans, it gives 8 points.\n\nChicken Hand is worth 8 points and is a catch-all for zero-fan hands that win.\n\nBut only if otherwise zero fans.\n\nCurrently, if I win, I will have:\n- One Voided Suit (1 point)\n- No Honors (1 point)\n- Possibly Single Wait or Closed Wait if applicable\n- Self Drawn if I draw the winning tile\n\nBut that\u2019s only 2-3 points \u2014 not enough.\n\nSo I need more.\n\nBut with the pung, I can't get many patterns.\n\nUnless I can get a dragon pung or something.\n\nBut I have no dragons.\n\nAnother idea: the across player has a concealed kong [CONCEALED x4] \u2014 possibly a kong they promoted.\n\nThey also have [B8,B8,B8] and [B6,B6,B6,B6] \u2014 so B6 kong.\n\nThey played BuGang W2 \u2014 added a W2 to a concealed pung to make a kong.\n\nSo they had [W2,W2,W2] concealed, then added a W2.\n\nSo W2 is involved.\n\nBut not helpful.\n\nBack to my discard.\n\nBest strategy: maximize winning chances.\n\nI have two strong draws:\n- T8: to complete [T7,T8,T9] chow\n- W6: to complete [W6,W7,W8] chow \u2014 but I can't because W7 and W8 are already used in [W7,W8,W9]\n\nCannot reuse tiles.\n\nSo the only possible new chow is:\n- [T1,T2,T3] \u2014 need T2,T3\n- [T7,T8,T9] \u2014 need T8\n- [W6,W7,W8] \u2014 impossible due to tile reuse\n- [W7,W8,W9] \u2014 already have\n\nSo only feasible new chow is [T7,T8,T9] or [T1,T2,T3]\n\n[T7,T8,T9] is better because I have two tiles.\n\nSo I should keep T7 and T9.\n\nAlso, I have W7 and W8 \u2014 if I can pair one, good.\n\nT1 is weakest \u2014 only one tile toward a chow.\n\nSo discard T1.\n\nThen, after discard, I have W7, W8, T7, T9.\n\nThen, if I draw T8, I can form [T7,T8,T9], and then I need a pair \u2014 so I must have two of W7/W8/T7/T9.\n\nCurrently, I have one each.\n\nSo I need to draw W7, W8, T7, or T9.\n\nT7 and T9 are more valuable because they can form the chow.\n\nBut after forming [T7,T8,T9], I have W7 and W8 \u2014 still no pair.\n\nSo I need to draw W7 or W8 to pair.\n\nW7 and W8 are both available (unshown:2 and 3).\n\nSo possible.\n\nIf I keep T1, I have less chance.\n\nMoreover, T1 is a terminal \u2014 if I win with a pung of T1, I could get Pung of Terminals or Honors (1 point), but I don't have a pung.\n\nSo no.\n\nTherefore, best move is to discard T1 to work toward [T7,T8,T9] chow and pair in W7 or W8.\n\nAmong the choices, Play T1 is the answer.\n\nAnswer: Play T1"}
